class:: HarmonicPeaks
summary:: Frequencies and magnitudes of associated harmonic partials
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks, Classes/Inharmonicity, Classes/Tristimulus, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Shared interpolated spectral peaks are associated with the nearest integer harmonic of the supplied F0. Only the strongest matching peak occupies each harmonic slot. Missing harmonics retain zero slots; an incorrect F0 or tight tolerance changes the result. The formulas are explicit MIRa conventions in the harmonic-descriptor tradition summarized by Peeters (2004); this is independent code, not a wrapper around another analysis library. Returns one frequency and raw FFT peak magnitude per harmonic index. Slot zero represents the fundamental even if it is absent.

Vanilla link::Classes/Pitch:: reports one fundamental. HarmonicPeaks exposes the measured partials associated with a supplied fundamental.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
FFT chain. This analyzer updates when a new frame arrives and holds its output between frames.

argument:: f0
Supplied fundamental in Hz, for example the first output of Pitch2. Nonpositive or invalid values disable harmonic association.

argument:: maxHarmonics
Literal number of harmonic slots from 1 through 64. Harmonic index is stable when partials are missing.

argument:: tolerance
Maximum distance in cents between a peak and its nearest integer multiple of f0, clamped from 0 through 600. Default 50.

argument:: peakThreshold
Minimum local-peak magnitude relative to the largest included spectral peak, from 0 through 1. Up to 128 strongest peaks are retained.

argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two from 256 through 8192, matching the FFT buffer. Frequency resolution and first-result latency depend on this size.

returns::
An Array containing frequency and magnitude Arrays, each maxHarmonics long.

method:: fromAudio
Convenience constructor: accepts audio and builds Pitch2 plus FFT internally, then calls kr with the estimated F0. The input range defaults to 55 through 1760 Hz, FFT size 4096 and hop fraction 0.25; it accepts the same harmonic controls. Use kr when sharing an existing pitch estimate or FFT chain.

examples::
HarmonicPeaks extracts the exact frequencies and amplitudes of up to code::maxHarmonics:: spectral partials associated with a fundamental frequency. In this example, it drives an additive sine bank spatializer: detected harmonic partials are synthesized as individual sinusoidal voices and spread across the stereo field from low order (left) to high order (right). An interactive code::MIRaGUI.bars:: displays the real-time energy distribution across all 16 harmonic partials.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 16);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var pitch = PitchMPM.kr(source, 80, 1600, 2048, 0.25);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var partials = HarmonicPeaks.kr(chain, pitch[0], 16, fftSize: 2048);
        var norm = (partials[1] / (partials[1].sum + 1e-6)).lag(0.04);

        var tones = Mix.fill(16, { |i|
            var freq = partials[0][i].clip(40, 10000);
            Pan2.ar(SinOsc.ar(freq, 0, norm[i] * 0.25 * (partials[0][i] > 30)), (i / 7.5) - 1.0)
        });
        var sound = (source * 0.2 ! 2) + tones;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, norm) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.bars("Harmonic Partials", ~miraBus, 16, 0.0, 0.6);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
